new id()
    .properties({
        title: 'central-thesis',
        type: 'compile',
        description: 'The Central Thesis of Cyberoptics',
        version: '0.1.0',
        status: 'editing',
        topic: 'cyberoptics',
    })
    .body(
        new Element('p').c('The Central Thesis of Cyberoptics'),
        new Header(2).c('1.0 - Cyberoptics: Examining Objects & Structural Properties'),
        `What a story is doing, is it is laying out a non-linear map, in linear-space. This is necessary, becuase in Cyberoptics, we study the Central Thesis: Human abilities are spectacular, only when they are understood properly and respect for their designed limitations. Form and Constraint is necessary for the balance of Power.`,
        `Though the linear-track is arrayed as a one-track-space, we are essentially "walking through" a forest; a non-linear space, and mapping out path-by-path, one-by-one. This means time is not reliably chronologically equivalent  in Cyberoptic Linear-space, as it is in Eventuality-space (Classical Chronology). This is iimportant, beucase if Einsteins General Relativity is accurate, then it means space and time are meshed together as a structure. This means that Dimension affects Time; in other words, when we "fill" in the map (in information space), so-to-speak, then Non-linear space is filled in almost like a "Torrent."`,
        new Header(2).c(`Introduction to "Operation Modes"`),
        `The Central Thesis in Cyberoptics focuses on three primary Features or "Operation Modes" of Human Neurology. This is Adjacent to Systems Construction (Cyberneering), but is not limited to Engineering; it's applications span deep to the very study and structure of information... more importantly; how we navigate information and facts of the world, properly.`,
        `We can build upwards and follow Linear-Continuity in Non-linear-space. This is the power of the Axiomata. It only emerges upwards by necessity (necessity over accessory.) 'Axiomata' is the mode we spend most of our time in, becuase it avoids Cyberoptic Tunnelling (which is powerful, and volatile; hazardous. See excavation further below.)'`,
        new Header(2).c(`Axiomata`),
        `Of these 3 Primary Modes, Cyberoptics begins with the most fundamental; ironically, the "Axiomata" is the beginnig fo Cyberoptic study, and it is consequently, the Foundational operation mode of the Human Cognitive and Neurological Processing System`,
        new Header(2).c(`Excavation`),
        `"Excavation" is the approach of Science. "Axiomata" is the approach of the Mathematician. "Orthogonal" is the approach of the Polymath. These are necessary to work in Unison, though not in parallel and not arbitrarily nor precisely; infact, this is another Core Discovery in Cyberoptics: We cannot navigate the world purely by Discovery nor Invention; we walk a tight, narrow, and straight path between Chaos and Order.`,
        `Excavation is concerned with the Dimension of "How" the world works. "How" Processes function. From the "Macro" to the "Iota". The Scientist however, is at risk of Excavating beyond reason. Without a Tether to the natural world, the Scientist risks analyzing the world of matter, of facts, of data, of rules, relationships and causality. This is, an undefined property of Information and Systmes; Analysis is indefinite and non-finite; infinite. Infinity within infinity within infinity; the gaps of fractalized Analysis fractures our Psyche and Sanity; our ability to make sense of the world in an integrated form `,
        new Header(2).c(`Communication as an Invariant of Systems.`),
        new Cell(`The Central Thesis of our Work in Cyberneering`),
        new Cell(`Ultimately the art of writing, thinking and structuring information; is the art of Communication, and Communication is the Backbone of Systems and Living things;`).chain([new Element('b').c(` Communication may even be the fundamental source of Order.`)]),
        new Cell(`This is somewhat supported by it's Antithesis: The opposite of Communication; Disarray, is almost Textbook-Entropy. And no System can Survive Un-managed Entropy... therefore, this is somewhat of an Axiom of `).inlink({ href: '#/cyberneering', text: 'Cyberneering.' }),
    ).write()
